Third party binaries in this directory
=======================================

These are gitignored and fetched by tool/fetch_proot.sh. They are not part of
the source tree and nothing here is linked into the app.


proot_exec.so, proot_loader.so
------------------------------
Termux proot 5.1.107.96, GPL-2.0-or-later
https://github.com/termux/proot

proot_exec.so is actually Termux's proot binary, renamed. Both are executed as
separate processes with execve, never dlopen'd and never linked against, so this
AGPL-3.0 application does not become subject to proot's GPL-2.0 terms. That is
the whole reason they are packaged as jniLibs and exec'd rather than vendored
into the Kotlin or C++ sources.

Packaged with useLegacyPackaging = true in android/app/build.gradle.kts. That
setting is load bearing: with the default the .so files stay compressed inside
the APK and there is no executable file on disk to execve.


libtalloc.so
------------
Termux libtalloc 2.5.0, LGPL-3.0-or-later
https://github.com/termux-packages/talloc

Copied next to proot as libtalloc.so.2, which is the SONAME proot's DT_NEEDED
actually asks for. LGPL in a separate process is fine, but the rename is what
keeps the dynamic linker satisfied without patching the binary.


libandroid-shmem.so
-------------------
Termux libandroid-shmem 0.7, BSD-3-Clause
https://github.com/termux-archive/packages


termux_pty.so
-------------
Built from source in android/app/src/main/cpp/termux_pty.cpp, which is derived
from the Termux app. GPL-3.0-or-later, and this project is AGPL-3.0, so the
terms are compatible and no exception is needed.

This one IS linked into the app, which is why it is built from source here rather
than downloaded. It is a thin JNI shim over posix_openpt, grantpt, unlockpt,
ptsname_r, fork, setsid, ioctl(TIOCSCTTY), ioctl(TIOCSWINSZ), dup2 and execve.


sha256
------
tool/proot_checksums.txt, verified on every fetch. The script refuses to run
without it and refuses to finish on a mismatch. Regenerate deliberately with
tool/fetch_proot.sh --write-checksums and review the diff.